# Project Rules & Standards

Refer to the following files in the `docs/` folder for all coding, architecture, and styling rules:

- **@docs/coding-standards.md** — TDD, DDD, project structure, secrets
- **@docs/architecture.md** — Tech stack, data flow, components
- **@docs/api-guidelines.md** — API contract, testing (100% coverage)
- **@docs/agents.md** — 3-agent architecture (Reader, Processor, Reporter)
- **@docs/persistence.md** — Storage separation, durability, retries
- **@docs/features.md** — Feature inventory and status
- **@docs/how-to-launch.md** — How to run backend and iOS app (simulator, device, HeyCyan)

## Architecture — Must Follow

- **Storage:** 2 collections — `meals` (happydiet), `diet_rules` (rules) — separate concerns.
- **3 agents:** Reader (image→text, persist); Processor (match, persist); Reporter (dashboard, compliance, audio).
- **Persistence:** Correct, durable writes; retries on failure; see persistence.md.

## Testing — Mandatory

- **Tests must always pass** before merge or deploy.
- **Unit + integration:** 100% coverage for `domain/` and `application/`.
- **E2E:** All HTTP endpoints covered.
- **Commands:** `npm test` (local), `npm run test:ci` (CI with JUnit).
- **After each feature:** Run `npm test`; do not continue if red.

## Meta Rule — Evolving Rules

When developing, we learn more rules. **Integrate them into the docs:**

- Add or update rules in `scope.md`, `design.md`, `agents.md`, `persistence.md`, `features.md`
- Keep docs in sync with implementation
- Update `tasks.md` when new work is identified
- Update this rule file if new standards emerge
